WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
The stories of Souls Games 
have always revolved around bosses,

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.740
but that statement has never been more true than for Dark Souls 3.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.480
If you understand who you're killing in this game, 
then you will understand the story.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.500
The first one in your way is Iudex Gundyr,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.460
the Ashen Judge 
and Scabbard to the Coiled Sword of the Shrine.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.640
This sword is bequeathed only to Chosen Ash 
who can best him in battle.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.020
But before he was the Ashen Judge, Gundyr walked through this place much like we did,

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.800
on his way to meet his firekeeper and link the fire.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.820
Charged with a duty, and granted a cast iron halberd 
that would never crumble,

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.040
Gundyr arrived... late,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.640
greeted by a shrine without fire,
and a bell that would not toll.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.320
The flame had already faded

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.280
and his firekeeper had been thrown 
into the depths of the Bell Tower,

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.460
grave of firekeepers' past.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.060
She never met her champion and the ensuing tragic farce,

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.640
became a favorite tale of the masses.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.980
And after he was bested by an unknown warrior, 
which is probably us,

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.220
Gundyr the Champion, 
became sheathed to a coiled sword

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.720
in the hope that some day 
the First Flame would be linked once more.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:21.200
Perhaps, Gundyr with his Unbreakable Halberd 
was fated to eternal service from the beginning.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.180
Since it is implied that Gundyr expected 
to meet a firekeeper,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.680
he was likely meant as a candidate for linking the fire.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.200
Those capable of linking the fire 
are named Lords of Cinder,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.860
beings capable of bringing back the world from the brink of darkness by linking the First Flame.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.740
Indeed, the game speaks of three Lords of Cinder 
who have already linked the fire,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.600
and they're being resurrected as a last resort, 
to link it once again.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.640
In the opening cutscene, you saw them:

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.640
Aldrich, Saint of the Deep

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.640
Yhrom, the Giant

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.560
and Farron's Abyss Watchers.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.020
Each of these Lords once had an Age of their own

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.640
and the remnants of their Age lives on in Dark Souls 3

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.480
and in their resurrection.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.560
For example, Aldrich is linked to these

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.640
bosses and their stories.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.640
The Abyss Watchers are linked here,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.500
and those in Lothric are conjoined here.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.796
For simplicity's sake, we are going to discuss these stories in three chunks starting with

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.740
Aldrich, Pontiff Sulyvahn, Vordt and the Dancer, 
who all reside in the Boreal Valley.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.220
The Boreal Valley is currently ruled over by 
Pontiff Sulyvahn,

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:32.880
a tyrant who sends his Outrider Knights to serve as his watchful eyes and his guards,

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.660
and the first knight of Pontiff Sulyvahn we meet is Vordt,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.824
an Outrider Knight who ambushes us 
as we attempt to leave Lothric.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.020
So, the Outrider Knights' job is to keep an eye on things

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.920
Sullivan's knights are also described as his 
"watchful eyes and his punitive blades"

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.280
Each Outrider Knight is provided with a ring 
by the Pontiff,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:59.360
which transforms them into frenzied beasts
 and lures them into battles of death.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.940
Specifically, the two main Outrider Knights we see upon the High Wall Of Lothric

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.980
appear at both points of progression in the area.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:12.140
So, perhaps they serve as strategically placed guards in order to hinder our progression

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.040
and for Sulyvahn to keep an eye on the world.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.320
When you went through Irithyll, I'm sure you noticed those ghosts that seem to be walking the streets.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:27.000
Well, they likely represent the Outrider Knights before their departure and descent into madness.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.520
Because two in particular are very interesting, 
they walk together: one man, one female.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.260
And the woman wears the mask of the Dancer.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:42.900
Vordt was never far from the fleeting Dancer, 
who watches over Emma in Lothric's Grand Cathedral.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.760
The Dancer is far more intriguing than Vordt is.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.800
The Pontiff ordered her to serve as a Dancer 
and then he ordered her to serve as his Outrider Knight.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.180
He bestowed enchanted swords upon her: 
one dark and one light, mirroring his own.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.840
Eventually, the Black eyes of the Pontiff 
transformed her into a beastly creature:

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.860
her gauntlets fusing with her own hide.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:11.920
The fascinating thing about the Dancer, though, is: 
who she was before she became Sulyvahn's pet.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:17.160
It's a very popular theory that she is one of the three daughters of Gwynevere, who appear in game

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:18.960
Here's the evidence:

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.780
Her Aurora Veil is said to be "An article of the old gods".

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:27.200
Which is permitted only for direct decedents of the old royal family.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:35.440
The Dancer's Soul can also be transposed, to give you the spell "Soothing Sunlight" - miracle of Gwynevere, of the old royalty

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:41.920
Gwynevere used to reside in Anor Londo, home of the gods,  and her line continues in Lothric.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.780
So Gwynevere was also revered as a goddess of fertility and bounty

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:53.800
she raised many heavenly children and the Dancer - having one of the three Sunlight spells - is clearly one of them.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:00.420
and of course, as you know, Pontiff Sulyvahn, the Tyrant, now rules over Irithyll and Anor Londo

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.180
So, it's my belief, that Sulyvahn gained power within Anor Londo

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:10.620
Then proclaimed himself pointiff and ordered Gwynevere's daughter to serve as his dancer

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:45.660
The sword in his left hand is a ceremonial sword, representing the judgement of the moon.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.280
Deep Protection tells us that the Deep was originally peaceful and secret place.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.600
Its deacons wearing dark red robes,

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.800
denoting their blessing of fire.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.420
Overtime, however,

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.980
the Deep became the final rest for many abhorrent things,

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.260
and indeed,

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.000
human dregs were likely some of those things

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.400
as the Dregs of Humanity are said

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.060
to sink to the lowest depths imaginable,

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.380
forming the bedrock of the world.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.700
Those who linger too long on the brink of the Deep

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.200
will often slip,

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.540
And lurking within the deep

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.200
are insects, which tear open the skin

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.200
and burrow into flesh.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.020
Eventually,

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.840
those dedicated to sealing away the horrors of the Deep

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.840
succumb to its very power.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:18.200
An example of this is their Tome of Knowledge,

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.580
which was originally intended to teach divine protection,

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.600
but it had dark tales added to its pages,

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.980
making it a thing most profane.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.480
And along with this descent,

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.560
presumably,

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.920
was Aldrich Saint of the Deep.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.720
"A right and proper cleric,

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.560
only he developed a habit of devouring men.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.100
He ate so many

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:46.640
that he bloated like a drowned pig,

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.080
then softened into sludge,

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.020
so they stuck him in the Cathedral of the Deep,

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.660
and they made him a Lord of Cinder,

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.020
not for virtue,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.900
but for might."

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.500
Aldrich was this simple saint,

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.100
who became a hugely powerful being

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.920
eventually chosen, maybe willingly and maybe not,

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.920
to become a Lord of Cinder,

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.320
and link the Fire.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.180
The Deacon Skirt tells us that the deacons

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.920
tended to the flame,

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:17.460
and

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.840
I'm, perhaps, inclined to believe that this meant that maybe

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.280
they were tending to the flame of Aldrich

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.980
when he was a Lord of Cinder.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.980
And whether this is true or not,

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.340
we do know that the deacons eventually

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.380
succumbed to the horrors of the Deep,

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.940
and neither tending to the flame nor the faith

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:35.960
can save them.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.500
You would have noticed that many deacons

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.460
cast Dark Soul Sorceries,

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:43.780
which were imparted to them by Archdeacon McDonnell.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.380
An adherent of Aldrich who was largely responsible

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.580
for the corruption of the deacons.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:54.020
Archdeacon McDonell delighted in the Cathedral's stagnating souls.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:58.100
For him, they represented the glorious bedrock of this world.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.380
Under the guidance of Archdeacon McDonnell,

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:04.840
these deacons became both clergymen and sorcerer.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.580
The Archdeacon's sin, as its called,

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.360
was to channel faith for sorcery,

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.360
which transformed his staff

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:14.960
from a symbol of religious authority

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.760
into a catalyst of dark sorceries.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.020
The deacons, they still had faith,

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:22.580
but it was not in fire any longer.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.600
It was in Aldrich, Saint of the Deep, their master.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.840
Upon his ressurection,

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:31.560
Aldrich, like many Lords of Cinder,

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.060
ruminated on the fading of the fire.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.600
For him, it inspired visions

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.420
He saw beyond the Age of Fire,

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.420
to the Age of Deep Waters

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.300
and the coming Age of the Deep Sea

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.660
Filled with new purpose,

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.140
he knew what he had to do.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.960
He would devour the gods himself.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.040
When we get to the Deacons of the Deep,

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.460
we expect to find Aldrich in his coffin,

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.420
but he's already left

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.420
for his home in the Borreal Valley.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.340
The deacons here are lead by Archdeacon Royce,

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.980
who is one the three archdeacons who remained behind

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.920
to keep eternal watch over his master's coffin,

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:11.560
hoping that one day he would return.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.720
Aldrich left behind a small doll in his coffin,

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.700
that Pontiff Sulyvahn gave to his most valued subjects.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.800
Wherever you go, the moon sets in Irithyll.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:25.100
Wherever you may be, Irithyll is your home.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.940
When Aldrich left, Archdeacon McDonnell went with him.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:33.440
We come across McDonnell in the depths of Anor Londo,

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.560
and McDonnell, like many other archdeacons, is obese.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.140
He's huge, and I see that as a legacy of Aldrich,

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:42.240
who derived power from gluttony;

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.680
they're clearly mimicking him.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.800
In Anor Londo, Archdeacon McDonnell came to lead the Aldrich Faithful

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.040
who are defenders, who exist

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:56.040
to ensure that Aldrich, Devourer of Gods, remains undisturbed.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.380
And when we come across Aldrich, we realise why

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.020
he wants to be undisturbed.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.580
Because Pontiff Sulyvahn,

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.180
with the Devourer of Gods by his side,

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.440
has imprisoned a God of the Old Royalty

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.160
in the Abandoned Cathedral

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.160
to be fed to the Devourer.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:15.160
Gwydolin, son of Gwyn and prior leader of the Dark Moon Knights,

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.280
was gradually devoured by Aldrich.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.620
As Aldrich slowly devoured the God of the Dark Moon,

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:21.620
He dreamt.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.080
In this dream, he saw the form of a pale girl in hiding,

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.080
and we know this is Yorshka,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.080
who is sister to Gwyndolin,

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.600
and a half-breed who is parallel to Priscilla from Dark Souls I,

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:35.380
but,

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.640
the interesting thing about this is the dream that Aldrich had

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.000
because apparently,

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.500
Aldrich only needs to dream about someone

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.440
to learn their skills

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.580
for he uses Priscilla's Lifehunt Scythe in battle,

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:51.600
and this fact that he can learn things through his visions,

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.860
has some interesting implications

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:57.720
because Aldrich is clearly wielding a Gravelord Greatsword

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.720
upon the end of his spear,

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.420
which lends credit towards this theory,

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:05.720
that Aldrich has devoured Nito in some capacity,

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.000
and he is called the Devourer of Gods, plural, after all.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.340
So another question becomes

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.780
"Did Aldrich also devour Nito?".

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:19.700
Well, he has the wispy Nito-like cloak with skulls within it, but

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.780
I think that it's more likely that the skulls are just remnants of humans he's devoured

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.740
You have to remember there is no concrete evidence

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.680
that he has devoured Nito.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.920
And I personally think

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:31.940
that it's more likely that

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:34.580
he simply dreamt up the Gravelord Spell

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:35.640
in a similar manner

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:39.000
to which he dreamt up the Lifehunt Scythe from Yorshka,

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.460
but what you think shapes the story here,

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.620
so let me know.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:47.820
So that's all of the pontiff's lackeys explain, for the most part.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:50.140
And the biggest unanswered questions here

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.040
to go into in other videos

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:56.640
is "What exactly the relationship between Sulyvahn and the deacons is?"

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:57.460
and

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:01.440
"In what order this story of corruption and treachery

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.140
played out?" because timeline is always one of the hardest things to get right

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.800
in the Souls Series,

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:09.560
but the biggest curiosity in my opinion

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:12.180
and the one that really, really interests me,

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:16.440
are Aldrich's visions of the Age of the Deep Sea

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.880
From a being, remember, that has visions so accurate

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.460
that he can learn spells from those visions.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:24.220
So,

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.100
in a franchise that's entirely self contained

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:30.260
within this Age of Fire and its cycles,

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.640
this, this vision of the Deep Sea

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.980
It's pretty much the only mention

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.660
of a different future,

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.820
and its appearance in these descriptions

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:40.920
feel so out of place, that I

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:45.120
almost expect it to be referenced in the future in some capacity,

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:48.060
assuming its not just a reference to Bloodborne.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.060
Maybe this indicates what Miyazaki

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:52.220
is doing next on one of his projects

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:52.760
or

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.760
maybe we'll se something related to this in the DLC.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.200
Moving on.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.280
Something set Sulyvahn down this path.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.500
When Sulyvahn was young sorcerer,

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.220
he discovered the Profaned Capital,

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.560
and down there, he discovered an unfading flame

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:10.820
below a distant tundra over Irithyll,

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.820
and when he found this,

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.560
a burning ambition took root within him.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.100
The Profaned Flame,

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.260
the origins of it aren't known,

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:21.900
but we do know a few things.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.900
We know it's an unfading flame;

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.900
we know that it can be manipulated,

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.940
and we know that it swallows the hearts of those who wield it.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.520
The pontiff himself imbued his greatsword with this fire,

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:36.240
and he also gave it to his holy knights.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.860
Shortly after he did this,

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:41.760
the Fire Witches had their heart swallowed by the flame

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.660
And as one last example of its corrupting influence,

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.900
the Handmaidens who wield it down at the Profaned Capital,

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.160
their dagger says that take pleasure

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.460
in wounding others,

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.860
And of course, the Pontiff himself

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:58.140
doesn't exactly have a good moral compass,

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:02.820
but apart from that, we know precious little about the Profaned Flame

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:06.380
and this has been the hardest part of the script to write for me

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:09.640
because the Profaned Flame defies all categorisation

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:12.680
as flames that have existed previously in the series.,

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.300
so I am going to work on my theories on it, and

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.900
while I'm doing that, I'll list those theories in the description

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:20.520
because I can talk about this thing for a very long time

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.740
without actually getting anywhere,

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:24.140
but the final thing,

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:27.360
and probably the most important thing we know about the Profaned Flame,

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.340
is that Yhorm the Giant

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.340
became a Lord of Cinder to put it to rest.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.440
Now, clearly, Yhorm was not successful

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.100
because the Profaned Flame has infiltrated

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.800
almost all of Irithyll,

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.380
and set a lot of events in motion.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:45.600
This just adds even more tragedy to Yhorm's tale.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.980
Yhorm is the descendant of an ancient conqueror,

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:53.080
and was asked by the very people once subjugated

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.200
to lead them,

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.200
serving as both a weighty blade

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.200
and a stone hard shield.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:01.420
Yhorm fought unflinchingly as a one-man vanguard,

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.400
but one day,

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.820
he lost the one he wished to protect.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:07.120
In response, he threw down his greatshield,

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:10.080
and added a left handed notch to his machete instead

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.560
so he could two-hand it

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.940
for he no longer had anything left to protect

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:20.020
All the while, his human subjects appeared quite disrespectful of him.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:22.240
They were insincere when they called him a lord,

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.740
and they doubted him.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.140
He is called Lonely Yhorm in his cinders,

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:30.620
and perhaps that's because he lost the one he wished to protect

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.820
or perhaps because he didn't have the love of his people.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:34.740
At some point,

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:38.480
the Profaned Flame became a real problem in the capital,

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.380
for according to his cinders,

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.020
Yhorm decided to sacrifice himself and

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:46.380
become a Lord of Cinder to put the Profaned Flame to rest.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.440
I don't know why Yhorm decided that

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.780
"Hey, I'm going to put out fire with fire.",

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.760
because when he did this,

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.760
fire rained down from the sky

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.100
and incinirated naught, but human flesh.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.100
This is an interesting insight into

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.680
who the linking of the Fire consumes.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.760
It consumed humans and humans alone,

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.360
and you see their disfigured, smelted corpses

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.360
all around Yhorm's chamber.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.400
Before he linked the fire, however,

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.380
Yhorm left behind two Stormrulers, which

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:22.900
was a legendary greatsword, also known as the Giant Slayer,

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:27.760
for the residual strength of storm that brings Giants to their knees,

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.760
so this thing could kill Giants

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.660
and one he gave to the humans who doubted him,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.220
he called them out on their cowardly words

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.620
and gave them a weapon capable of killing him,

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:42.620
and the other Stromruler, he gave to a dear friend in return for a promise.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.760
This dear friend was Siegward,

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.760
who journeys to the Profaned Capital

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:48.400
in order to uphold his promise

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.640
and slay his old friend.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:51.900
Presumably,

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.120
Yhorm asked Siegward to kill him

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.120
if he ever betrayed his duty,

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:58.120
and Siegward does so,

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:02.080
seeing that Yhorm has not returned to link the Fire once again.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:05.280
The Profaned Capital also had its sorcerers

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:08.660
who claimed heirship to the legacy of the renowned scholar,

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.800
Big Hat Logan,

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.760
even going so far as to emulate the type of staff he used.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:15.340
But halfway across the world,

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.920
I know of two Crystal Sages

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.600
who emulated him even more closely.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:22.940
These Crystal Sages served as spiritual guides

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:26.100
to the scholars of Lothric's Grand Archives,

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:29.800
and one of them went on to ally with the Undead Legion.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:34.100
The Undead Legion of Farron was a caravan of Undead

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.520
dedicated to the eradication of the Abyss

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.340
wherever it was found.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.580
The Abysswatchers, as they were called,

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:45.240
follow the duty and the form of the Wolf Knight of Dark Souls I,

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.640
known as Artorias the Abysswalker.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.980
They are essentially his legacy.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.260
They made their home in Farron Keep,

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:54.440
and high above Farron Keep,

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.700
lies an emaciated old wolf.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:59.700
The Abbyswatchers, for their hunting of the Abyss,

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:03.960
they required some art that went beyond any existing art.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:08.540
Wolf's Blood, the legacy of Artorias, provided just that.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.920
Their pointed steel helm became shirked

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.600
as this sinister omen by the masses

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:15.500
because,

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:20.340
think about it, if you saw that pointed steel helmet coming towards your kingdom,

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.900
you knew you were in trouble

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.520
'cause these guys are dedicated to taking out the Abyss,

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.240
and indeed their home in Farron

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.320
might just be set above such a kingdom,

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.500
for below are the Catacombs of Carthus,

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:38.320
and sealed within a goblet, deep below in the catacombs

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.100
is the encounter with High Lord Wolnir,

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.880
a ruler who succumbed to the Abyss.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:47.540
Before succumbing to the Abyss, Wolnir was a conqueror.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:50.620
He ruled over the people of Carthus of the Sands,

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:53.800
formidable warriors who were masters of the curved sword

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:58.600
and also of pyromancies that enhanced the effectiveness of their curved swords

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:01.740
The swordsmen attached great value to victory

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:05.700
at all costs, for where was the honour in death?

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:08.920
They lived for their High Lord Wolnir,

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:12.420
who was conqueror of most lands known to their people, and

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.580
yeah, you can see why they loved him.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.840
In Wolnir's time,

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:20.340
there were other lords who had their crowns rightful bequeathed upon them,

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:23.080
but Wolnir brought them to their knees and

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.120
ground their crowns to dust,

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.720
forming his own crown from theirs

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.380
for he was the one high lord

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.600
keen to outlive all others,

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.280
reminds me a lot of what we did in Dark Souls Two.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:38.320
Anyway, somehow Wolnir himself

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:40.180
fell to the Abyss, and

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:43.140
he was gripped by this fear of true darkness

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.480
and he pleaded to the gods for the first time

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.320
In our boss fight with him,

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.320
there is a darkness below Wolnir,

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:53.020
and it's struggling to consume him,

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:55.620
but Wolnir had his Holy Sword

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:59.960
and he had three armlets that he stripped from the corpses of clerics

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:03.680
and these things gave him some resemblance of comfort.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:06.020
Of course, we destroy the bracelets,

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:09.120
and the Abyss finally consumes him.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:13.960
While he was in the Abyss, however, Wolnir was not inactive.

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:19.240
Black Serpent is this pyromancy that was discovered from the Abyss by Wolnir

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:23.700
which went on to inspire the black arts of his grave wardens .

00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:26.580
The Grave Warden Pyromancy Tome was developed

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:30.300
by his grave wardens who discovered his pyromancies

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:32.440
And going back up for a second,

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:36.680
Wolnir and the Abyss, their proximity to the Abysswatchers

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:38.680
probably isn't coincidence.

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:42.040
In fact, it makes quite a lot of sense for Carthus

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:45.420
to be one of the kingdoms the Abysswatchers toppled.

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:50.660
So, let's go back up to the Abysswatchers for a second and see if this theory holds any weight.

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:54.320
Eventually, the Abysswatchers became Lords of Cinder.

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:57.780
Their shared Wolf's Blood served their mandate as lords,

00:22:57.780 --> 00:22:59.780
essentially, it meant the requirements.

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:03.940
To gain access to the Abysswatchers, you have to extinguish three flames,

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:06.500
and I've always wondered why this ritual existed.

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:09.500
It felt very video gamey and out of place,

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:15.300
but I went through once more recently and I looked really closely at the engravings behind each flame.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:20.480
One looks like the Four Kings, one looks like Nito, and one looks like the Bed of Chaos,

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:22.860
three of the main lords in Dark Souls One,

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:29.500
and these were the souls you had to collect to gain access to Gwyn and open a giant stone door, so

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:33.040
these are likely here to symbolise that, right?

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:37.680
We're extinguishing three flames and we're opening the door, that explains the ritual.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.880
Anyway, that's more a piece of trivia than anything.

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:44.200
After the Legion's Watchers became Lords of Cinder,

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:46.200
the Wolf Blood dried up,

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:49.240
and Farron was consumed by a festering wood

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:51.080
Dark Wraiths began to roam.

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:53.320
The Keep fell to ruins, and

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.640
as suggested by many of you in my lorethrough,

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:01.080
the Abysswatchers after upon resurrected to link the Fire once more

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:04.200
may have been affected by the Abyss as well.

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:05.980
So here's the theory,

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:09.140
the Abysswatchers were driven to seek out the Abyss, right?

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:12.280
Well, what if, upon they ressurection,

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:15.180
the Abyss far below in the Catacombs of Carthus

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:18.100
crept into the Abysswatchers themselves?

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:23.580
This would explain why the Abysswatchers are locked in endless combat with themselves

00:24:23.580 --> 00:24:27.760
because they're driven to seek out the Abyss, but they also can't die

00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:30.240
so they're locked in endless combat.

00:24:30.400 --> 00:24:34.600
When I read this theory in the commends, something else clicked as well.

00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:38.980
the Wolf Knight Armour, which belonged to Artorias who fell to the Abyss,

00:24:38.980 --> 00:24:41.940
says that the armour of the Abysswatchers

00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:44.700
suggests their own eventual end.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:45.600
So,

00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:47.960
the game is drawing a parallel here

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:51.320
beteween Artorias and the Abysswatchers. It's saying that

00:24:51.320 --> 00:24:56.360
the armour of the Abysswatchers shows that they're falling to the Abyss as well.

00:24:56.500 --> 00:24:58.660
And here's the really interesting thing,

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:00.660
when you look closely at their armour,

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:04.920
you realise it has black tendrils of the Abyss rising up

00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:08.520
so the armour is showing us that they fell to the Abyss...

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:09.720
probably.

00:25:09.720 --> 00:25:13.560
This theory isn't concrete and no one should take it as such,

00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:16.840
but I think it's the best explanation for their in-fighting.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:19.220
It's my favourite explanation anyway,

00:25:19.220 --> 00:25:22.800
and mostly, this one was all you guys, so thank you. :)

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:26.720
Onwards to Lothric,

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:29.400
the knights of Lothric were hunters of dragons,

00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:33.140
explaining their affinity with lightning and why they worshipped the Sun.

00:25:33.500 --> 00:25:35.980
They have since tamed dragons and

00:25:35.980 --> 00:25:40.260
with their drakes, they once crushed anything that threatened their shores

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:44.420
The knight has served as one of the three pillar of Lothric since Ancient Times,

00:25:44.420 --> 00:25:48.700
and it shares place along side the Wyverns as a symbol of Lothric.

00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:52.400
However, tales of dragons layers are now a rare thing

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:56.980
and they're told only in fragments and in whispers in remote regions.

00:25:56.980 --> 00:26:00.200
The Dragonslayer Armour lost its master long ago,

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:04.280
but it still remembers the sporting hunts they shared together.

00:26:05.220 --> 00:26:06.620
When we fight against it,

00:26:06.620 --> 00:26:09.720
the armour retains its master's fighting style,

00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:13.900
but now it has a new master, the Pilgrim Butterfly

00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:17.340
Now the Soul of the Dragonslayer Armour

00:26:17.340 --> 00:26:20.360
is the only mention of these butterfly creatures,

00:26:20.360 --> 00:26:23.740
so speculation abounds whenever you talk about them.

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:25.740
When you look up at them closely, though,

00:26:25.740 --> 00:26:28.220
closer than the game intends you to ever get,

00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:30.440
you'll see that they're flesh and bone

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:34.960
and they're almost bent backwards with a ribcage jutting outwards.

00:26:35.060 --> 00:26:38.620
Now, their name is one of the biggest clues we have,

00:26:38.620 --> 00:26:42.780
and the word pilgrim makes me think of the Pilgrims of Londor,

00:26:42.780 --> 00:26:45.880
who all died on their way to the peak of Lothric.

00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:47.660
And just like these pilgrims,

00:26:47.660 --> 00:26:51.880
these Pilgrim Butterflies fly upwards to the peak of Lothric, as well.

00:26:51.880 --> 00:26:56.080
And in both these cases, with the Pilgrims and the Pilgrim Butterflies,

00:26:56.080 --> 00:26:59.880
we have no real idea why either of them are going up

00:26:59.880 --> 00:27:04.140
so perhaps we'll learn more if ever we get Londor-themed DLC, and

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:05.740
I think that's pretty likely.

00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:10.180
I'm going to list two other theories in the description about the Butterflies

00:27:10.180 --> 00:27:13.440
because the bottom line is we don't know what they are.

00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:15.600
Next is the Archives,

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:20.360
and beyond the Archives is Prince Lothric and his brother, Lorian.

00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:21.560
Curiously,

00:27:21.560 --> 00:27:23.620
these are the only Lords of Cinder

00:27:23.620 --> 00:27:28.460
who were not featured in the opening cutscene of lords being ressurected,

00:27:28.460 --> 00:27:31.900
and I believe, that's because they never linked the Fire,

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:32.980
and I think

00:27:32.980 --> 00:27:39.240
their rejection of linking the Fire might have been what set all of the desperate resurrections into motion.

00:27:39.680 --> 00:27:44.860
This is just a theory, but I think it's backed up by most of these descriptions and this dialogue:

00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:00.960
So there's Prince Lothric and Lorian, his brother.

00:28:00.960 --> 00:28:03.920
Lorian is the eldest and before he was crippled,

00:28:03.920 --> 00:28:07.600
he was a knight who single-handedly slayed a Demon Prince,

00:28:07.600 --> 00:28:11.020
the victory eternally scorching his sword with flame.

00:28:11.240 --> 00:28:17.380
The Cinders of A Lord states that the Lothric Bloodline was obsessed with creating a worthy heir.

00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:23.660
They needed someone to link the Flame, and for some reason, Lorian did not suffice,

00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:27.660
so they put their faith in the next born, Prince Lothric.

00:28:27.900 --> 00:28:31.440
As his throne states, "last hope of his line"

00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:35.620
Prince Lothrics, destined to be a Lord of Cinder,

00:28:35.620 --> 00:28:39.320
was born into swaddling clothes used in ancient prayer

00:28:39.320 --> 00:28:41.640
and they are all that he has ever worn.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:44.000
He was cherished by the Royal Family

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:46.120
despite being born into illness,

00:28:46.120 --> 00:28:48.120
a frail and shrivelled child.

00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:52.160
He was their last hope and meant to be a champion,

00:28:52.340 --> 00:28:55.380
but some things will remain distant dreams forever.

00:28:55.860 --> 00:28:58.240
Linking the Fire proved impossible,

00:28:58.240 --> 00:29:01.780
so the family resorted to unspeakable means

00:29:01.780 --> 00:29:06.720
Descriptions don't say or imply what these unspeakable means are,

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:09.000
so that's up to us to guess that.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:11.700
But after mentioning these unspeakable means,

00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:14.700
the Cinder description goes on to say that

00:29:14.700 --> 00:29:18.400
the path to linking the Fire is a cursed one indeed.

00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:22.280
So Prince Lothric was cursed. With what? We don't know,

00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:25.040
but Lorian embraced his brother's curse,

00:29:25.040 --> 00:29:27.180
leaving him mute and crippled.

00:29:27.440 --> 00:29:30.480
It is said that Lorian, the one who embraced the Curse,

00:29:30.480 --> 00:29:33.560
did so willingly and embraced his fate.

00:29:33.760 --> 00:29:37.760
When we kill Lorain in the boss fight, Lothric ressurects him, saying,

00:29:37.760 --> 00:29:39.360
"For that is our curse."

00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:44.180
So maybe being unable to die itself is the Fire Linking Curse,

00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:45.760
and why he says,

00:29:55.540 --> 00:30:01.840
After becoming one, the Souls of the Twin Princes says that they rejected their duty to become Lords of Cinder

00:30:01.840 --> 00:30:06.860
and settled down far, far away to watch the fire fade from a distance.

00:30:06.860 --> 00:30:09.960
The curse has made their souls nearly inseparable.

00:30:09.960 --> 00:30:15.680
So, why did Lothric grow to despise and reject his duty as a Lord of Cinder?

00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:20.880
Well, it's very likely due to a man named as the First of the Scholars,

00:30:20.880 --> 00:30:22.680
Soul Stream says that

00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:26.300
he was alleged to be a private mentor of the Royal Prince

00:30:26.300 --> 00:30:29.080
and that he doubted the Linking of the Fire.

00:30:29.080 --> 00:30:31.620
So, it's very likely that this scholar

00:30:31.620 --> 00:30:35.940
was the one who made Lothric reject his fate as a Lord of Cinder,

00:30:35.940 --> 00:30:38.640
and there is so much more to the tale of Lothric,

00:30:38.640 --> 00:30:40.000
but we don't have time.

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:42.540
I want to talk about the kingdom, about the royal family,

00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:45.240
but this video is only about the main bosses, so

00:30:45.240 --> 00:30:47.240
I still have to mention Oceiros

00:30:47.240 --> 00:30:49.800
king of Lothric, and his wife, the queen,

00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:53.940
so please subscribe and look out for the optional bosses lore video.

00:30:55.220 --> 00:30:59.340
And the final main boss, the being we fight after the Firekeeper

00:30:59.340 --> 00:31:02.400
chastises the lords for going without thrones

00:31:02.400 --> 00:31:04.660
is the Soul of Cinder itself,

00:31:04.660 --> 00:31:08.220
located within the Kiln of the First Flame.

00:31:08.480 --> 00:31:12.860
The Soul of Cinder if actually a fairly easy being to explain.

00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:16.120
Ever since Gwyn, the first Lord of Cinder,

00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:19.120
many exalted lords have linked the First Flame,

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:24.340
and it is their very Souls that have manifested themselves as Defender of the Flame

00:31:25.160 --> 00:31:28.540
The Soul of Cinder is their deific manifestation

00:31:28.540 --> 00:31:32.020
More specifically, it's clear that the Soul of Cinder is this

00:31:32.020 --> 00:31:34.600
conglomerate of players themselves,

00:31:34.600 --> 00:31:38.520
us from previous games and cycles who have linked the fire.

00:31:38.740 --> 00:31:41.800
Using the Ninja Flip Ring from Dark Souls One,

00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:45.460
curved swords, pyromancies, sorceries, miracles

00:31:45.460 --> 00:31:47.100
and in phase two,

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:51.540
the music shifts to this twisted tribute of Gwyn's theme

00:31:51.540 --> 00:31:54.680
as he takes on the First Lord's fighting style.

00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:59.960
The Kiln also, it represents the state of the world if you look behind you.

00:31:59.960 --> 00:32:03.660
It's a city twisted and distorted and folded in on itself,

00:32:03.660 --> 00:32:08.020
just like the entire game and bosses we just journeyed through.

00:32:08.020 --> 00:32:12.200
Dark Souls Three contains the histories, the people and the lands of

00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.740
of the Abysswatcher's Age,

00:32:13.740 --> 00:32:16.140
of the Pontiff and Aldrich's Age,

00:32:16.140 --> 00:32:17.720
of Yhorm's Age, and

00:32:17.720 --> 00:32:20.240
the story of Lothric that literally

00:32:20.240 --> 00:32:23.260
seems to have called forth old Lords of Cinder

00:32:23.260 --> 00:32:25.260
to link the Fire once again.

00:32:25.540 --> 00:32:28.080
And as you stand in front of the Flame,

00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:30.100
four choices lay before you,

00:32:30.100 --> 00:32:32.100
more than any previous game,

00:32:32.100 --> 00:32:35.080
